    "text": "Brian is an Irish god. The popular Irish name comes from him. He belonged to the Tuatha Dé Danann and was one of the tragic Sons of Tuireann. His mother was the goddess Danu. His father was the hero Tuireann. Brian and his two brothers ambushed Cian, the father of Lugh. Cian changed into a pig, but the brothers killed him. Lugh made them complete eight impossible feats. They finished seven and failed the last, so Lugh slew them. The name also belongs to the high king Brian Boru. He rose from a tiny kingdom to rule all Ireland. He died at Clontarf while gathering forces against the Vikings.",
